    "max_result_json_nodes": 500000,
    "max_result_json_depth": 33,
    "min_dimension_m": 0.001,
    "max_dimension_m": 100000,
    "max_aspect_ratio": 20,
    "max_point_offset_to_min_dimension": 20
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "Synthetic signed uniform density-contrast response only; no reference field, observation correction, inversion, uncertainty propagation or geological uniqueness.",
    "All prism bounds and points share one declared local Cartesian metre frame with x/y/up axes and height datum; caller transforms upstream.",
    "bounds_m order is xmin,xmax,ymin,ymax,zmin,zmax, all increasing. gx/gy follow local axes; g_down=-gz_up.",
    "Negative Newtonian potential is zero at infinity. Backend positive potential is negated; downward g_z is converted to gz_up.",
    "Potential and acceleration are finite at centres/interiors/faces/edges/corners; no tensor/gradient components are requested. Overlapping signed prisms superpose.",
    "Each prism uses its original lower corner as local origin before backend calls, preserving represented bounds/point differences. Conservative dimension/aspect/point-offset conditioning bounds reject unsupported far/thin analytic-corner evaluations without a hidden approximation. Numerical budgets do not guarantee geological accuracy.",
    "Sensitivities are unit-density responses at fixed bounds/points, in output units per kg/m^3, including zero-density sources. No geometry derivatives or propagated uncertainty.",
    "Harmonica and Choclo versions and G are checked. JavaScript validates portable requests but numerical execution requires the Python potential-fields extra."
  ],
  "references": [
    "https://www.fatiando.org/harmonica/v0.7.0/api/generated/harmonica.prism_gravity.html",
    "https://www.fatiando.org/choclo/v0.3.2/api/generated/choclo.prism.gravity_pot.html",
    "https://physics.nist.gov/cuu/Constants/Table/allascii.txt"
  ]
